**Equiangular (AAA)**: at least two pairs of equal corresponding angles, which makes the third pair equal by the angle sum.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large},scale=0.85]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (0.827,1.773);
\draw (A) -- (B) -- (C) -- cycle;
\pic[draw,"$\alpha$",angle radius=0.38cm,angle eccentricity=1.7] {angle=B--A--C};
\pic[draw,"$\beta$",angle radius=0.45cm,angle eccentricity=1.7] {angle=C--B--A};
\coordinate (A2) at (4.2,0);
\coordinate (B2) at (8.36,0);
\coordinate (C2) at (5.523,2.837);
\draw (A2) -- (B2) -- (C2) -- cycle;
\pic[draw,"$\alpha$",angle radius=0.55cm,angle eccentricity=2.0] {angle=B2--A2--C2};
\pic[draw,"$\beta$",angle radius=0.65cm,angle eccentricity=2.0] {angle=C2--B2--A2};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**SSS**: three pairs of corresponding sides in the same ratio.

[tikz]
