\coordinate (P) at (1.6,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (1.377,1.966);
\draw (V) -- (P) node[midway,below] {$a$};
\draw (V) -- (Q) node[midway,above left] {$b$};
\draw (P) -- (Q);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.45cm,angle eccentricity=2.0] {angle=P--V--Q};
\coordinate (V2) at (4.2,0);
\coordinate (P2) at (6.6,0);
\coordinate (Q2) at (6.265,2.949);
\draw (V2) -- (P2) node[midway,below] {$ka$};
\draw (V2) -- (Q2) node[midway,above left] {$kb$};
\draw (P2) -- (Q2);
\pic[draw,"$\theta$",angle radius=0.6cm,angle eccentricity=2.0] {angle=P2--V2--Q2};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

**RHS**: both triangles right-angled, with the hypotenuses and another pair of corresponding sides in the same ratio.

